.TH "KBLUEPROXIMITY.SERVICE" "8" "September 27, 2026" "Marco Faenzi" ""
.SH NAME
kblueproximity.service \- systemd user unit for kblueproximity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemctl --user enable --now kblueproximity.service
.br
.B systemctl --user disable --now kblueproximity.service
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kblueproximity.service
is a user service unit for running
.BR kblueproximity (1)
inside the user systemd manager.
.PP
The package installs this unit but does not enable or start it automatically.
Users must opt in explicitly.
.SH EXAMPLES
Enable and start for the current user:
.IP
.B systemctl --user enable --now kblueproximity.service
.PP
Stop and disable for the current user:
.IP
.B systemctl --user disable --now kblueproximity.service
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kblueproximity (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.unit (5)
